          "text": "{\"target_translation\":\"I love you.\",\"dimensions\":{\"T\":{\"score\":4,\"evidence_status\":\"assessable\",\"confidence\":0.99,\"reason\":\"Nikki directly avows love as a present emotional state. The narration explicitly characterizes the utterance as an honest admission.\",\"evidence\":[{\"block_id\":\"target\",\"quotation\":\"I love you\"},{\"block_id\":\"scene\",\"quotation\":\"The admission felt like a release, a moment of pure honesty that left them both vulnerable but deeply connected.\"}]},\"P\":{\"score\":0,\"evidence_status\":\"assessable\",\"confidence\":0.93,\"reason\":\"The focal expression contains no promise, proposal, or specified undertaking by Nikki. Its intimate setting and Keith's reciprocal response establish mutual affection, but affection and reciprocity alone do not make Nikki's avowal a commitment.\",\"evidence\":[{\"block_id\":\"target\",\"quotation\":\"I love you\"},{\"block_id\":\"scene\",\"quotation\":\"Keith stilled, then smiled. “I love you too,” he said, his voice steady and sincere.\"}]},\"E\":{\"score\":3,\"evidence_status\":\"assessable\",\"confidence\":0.96,\"reason\":\"Besides avowing love, the expression is represented as a spontaneous affective outpouring: it emerges suddenly and involuntarily, before Nikki can restrain it. This substantially supports expressive-discharge force.\",\"evidence\":[{\"block_id\":\"scene\",\"quotation\":\"“I love you,” she said suddenly, the words spilling out before she could stop them.\"}]},\"O\":{\"score\":0,\"evidence_status\":\"assessable\",\"confidence\":0.91,\"reason\":\"The expression's core force is adequately captured by the truth-presenting avowal and its spontaneous expressive discharge. The evidence does not establish a distinct residual function.\",\"evidence\":[{\"block_id\":\"target\",\"quotation\":\"I love you\"},{\"block_id\":\"scene\",\"quotation\":\"The admission felt like a release, a moment of pure honesty\"}]}},\"original_speech_situation\":\"After Nikki and Keith have sex and are lying together in bed, Nikki turns to him with her heart described as full and spontaneously says “I love you.” Keith pauses, smiles, and reciprocates the avowal.\",\"affection_evidence\":\"present\",\"undertaking_and_uptake\":\"The focal expression does not specify an undertaking. Keith receives the avowal positively and reciprocates with “I love you too,” followed by another kiss, but this is uptake of an avowal rather than acceptance of a defined promise or commitment.\",\"recognised_work\":false,\"recognition_note\":\"I do not recognize the supplied text as a particular known work.\",\"limitations\":\"The supplied scene strongly supports the utterance's avowal and spontaneous expressive character, but it does not establish any precise relational commitment arising from Nikki's words. Later material cannot by itself supply unstated terms to this utterance.\"}"
